{"author":"schacon+claude-opus@gmail.com","body":"FINAL: c4cf72948 committed on grit-t5-progress; 7/8 passing (was 4/8). Remaining test 3 'no shallow lines after receiving ACK ready' needs full v0 stateless-RPC multi-round negotiation: send have batches in separate POSTs WITHOUT done, read 'ACK <oid> common/ready' responses, feed back to negotiator, and when 'no-done' is negotiated + server returns 'ready' skip 'done' entirely. Also needs fetch-pack-labelled trace lines (test greps 'fetch-pack< ACK .* ready' and '! fetch-pack> done'). Current fetch_pack_v0_v1_stateless_http sends all haves+done in one POST so server never emits 'ready'. Confirmed via curl the real server (system git-http-backend) ACKs haves as 'common' and only says 'ready' after enough common base across rounds. Left open: substantial v0-negotiation rewrite, high regression risk to other t5 HTTP fetch tests; deferred to avoid grinding one subtest at expense of the rest."}